---
description: Follow the repo's AGENTS.md, decisions, CONTRIBUTING, hooks, and CI
alwaysApply: true
---
Before starting work or asking the user anything, read in order: the repo's agent guide, its binding
rules / decisions file, the repo's `STATE.md` and this branch's `STATE-<slug>.md` (repo root), then
the project's notes folder in the shared store
(`<Projects>\_claude\Claude Projects\Working Memory\memory\<project>\INDEX.md`). If a rule or note
already answers a question, act on it and cite it; never ask what the rules answer.
Tiers (decision 2026-11-22): the repo holds the router AGENTS.md, SPEC, DECISIONS, rules, data and live
state (STATE.md, STATE-<slug>.md committed on its branch, BACKLOG.md, archives/); the store folder holds
notes only (preferences, machine facts, gotchas); TASK.md is git-ignored per worktree.
At 80% context, run state-closeout (closeout mode); on-demand handoff: state-closeout handoff. No
HANDOFF/handoffs files; STATE-<slug> is the handoff. A PR's last commit archives the state file.
Store unreachable (PC offline, cloud session): live state is still in the repo; only notes are missing.
Before changing anything in a repo, read and follow its AGENTS.md, decisions, CONTRIBUTING.md, hooks (.pre-commit-config.yaml, core.hooksPath, .git/hooks), and CI workflows. Their rules and decisions still bind.
Never bypass a hook or gate without the user's explicit yes: no --no-verify, no skipping CI, no
direct pushes of generated or bot-owned files. Branch + PR, never force-push, one repo at a time.
If an older agent doc's layout differs from the workstation-core template, that layout is migrated into the template, keeping every rule; a layout difference is not a blocker or a reason to stop.

Before driving the harness.design desktop app, hold the per-PC harness.design lock: see section 5b of `<Projects>\active\workstation\instructions\projects-AGENTS.md` ("harness.design lock"). Acquire before use, check in at least every 10 min, and release when done. Never delete the lock file by hand. MCP cloud tools do not need the lock. An agent delete goes through the desktop app under the lock.
